# Ascendo Production Timesheet — Changelog

## How to add to GitHub
1. Go to your GitHub repo
2. Click **Add file → Create new file**
3. Name it `CHANGELOG.md`
4. Paste this content in
5. Click **Commit changes**

---

## Version History

---

### v4 — Timezone Fix
**Files changed:** `public/index.html`, `api/log.js`

**Problem:** Clock in/out times were being recorded in US time (UTC) instead of Australian local time, because the Vercel server is hosted in Washington DC.

**Fix:** All time formatting is now done in the browser (which knows the local timezone) before being sent to the server. The server no longer formats any times — it simply writes whatever it receives directly to the Google Sheet.

---

### v3 — Unlimited Breaks & New Employees
**Files changed:** `public/index.html`, `api/log.js`, `api/sessions.js`

**Changes:**
- Added employees **Jamie** and **Wendy** to the roster
- Replaced separate Break 1/2/3 columns in the Google Sheet with a single **Breaks Detail** summary column (e.g. `B1: 09:00 AM–09:15 AM (15m), B2: 12:30 PM–01:00 PM (30m)`)
- This allows unlimited breaks per shift with no column limit
- Hours Worked still correctly deducts all break time regardless of how many breaks are taken

---

### v2 — Multiple Breaks Support
**Files changed:** `public/index.html`, `api/log.js`

**Problem:** The app only supported a single lunch break per shift.

**Changes:**
- Replaced "Lunch Break" with a general **Break** system
- Employees can now take unlimited breaks in a single shift
- Each break is tracked with a start and end time
- Break history is shown in the action panel during a shift
- Google Sheet stored up to 3 breaks in separate columns (later replaced in v3)
- CSV export includes all break times and total break duration
- Hours Worked automatically deducts total break time

---

### v1.2 — NaN Fix in Hours Worked
**Files changed:** `public/index.html`, `api/log.js`

**Problem:** The Hours Worked column in Google Sheets was showing NaN (Not a Number).

**Cause:** When clocking out, the server was trying to calculate hours using the formatted time string stored in the sheet (e.g. "09:30 AM") instead of the original precise timestamp. JavaScript cannot do maths on formatted time strings.

**Fix:** The app now sends the original ISO timestamp (`clockIn`) along with the clock-out event, so the server always has the raw timestamps needed for accurate calculation.

---

### v1.1 — Google Sheets Integration
**Files changed:** `api/log.js`, `api/sessions.js`, `public/index.html`

**Changes:**
- Connected the app to Google Sheets via a Google Service Account
- Every clock event (clock in, break start, break end, clock out) writes to the **TimeLog** tab in real time
- The app syncs from the sheet on load and every 60 seconds, keeping multiple tablets in sync
- Local browser storage used as a cache so the app still works if internet drops temporarily
- Google Sheet columns: Employee, Date, Day, Clock In, Lunch Out, Lunch In, Clock Out, Hours Worked, Lunch Duration, Status, Last Updated

---

### v1.0 — Initial Build
**Files created:** `public/index.html`, `api/log.js`, `api/sessions.js`, `vercel.json`, `package.json`

**Features:**
- Tablet-friendly employee time tracker hosted on Vercel
- Employees: Augustina, Hong, Lily, Shina
- Clock In → Lunch Break → End Lunch → Clock Out workflow
- Live clock display with local date
- Time log table with weekly filter
- CSV export for weekly timesheets
- Data stored in Google Sheets via serverless API functions
- App adds to tablet home screen and runs like a native app

---

## Infrastructure

| Component | Details |
|---|---|
| Hosting | Vercel (auto-deploys from GitHub on every commit) |
| Repo | github.com/raymondwchong/Ascendo-Production-Timesheet |
| Data | Google Sheets — TimeLog tab |
| Auth | Google Service Account (credentials stored as Vercel environment variables) |
| Environment Variables | `GOOGLE_SHEET_ID`, `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` |

